    "sub_firstblock": "The general setup of the theoretical framework is as follows. The model has two periods, $t = [ 1 , 2 ]$ . In the first period $t = 1$ , productivity and skills are realized, and firms make their decisions. Specifically, at the beginning of the first period firms draw a random firm productivity level and managers draw a skill level; the best manager at the firm assumes the job of the CEO. At the middle of the period, existing firms decide whether to continue operations or exit the market. After the exit decisions are made, continuing firms make hiring decisions; firms can fire their existing managers and search for a replacement. At the beginning of the second period $t = 2$ the managerial labor market clears. Exiting firms are potentially replaced by new firms. Output is realized and wages are paid. "
